## Summary

I successfully implemented comprehensive tests for checkbox recognition (task 2.2) following TDD principles. The tests cover:

**Core checkbox patterns:**
- `- [ ]` (incomplete with spaces)
- `- []` (incomplete without spaces)  
- `- [x]` and `- [X]` (complete, case-insensitive)
- `- [!]` (failed)

**Edge cases and variations:**
- Leading whitespace (spaces, tabs, mixed)
- Non-checkbox bullets that should be ignored
- Checkboxes with no description text
- Multiple checkboxes in one line
- Special markdown characters in descriptions
- Checkboxes in inline code (edge case documentation)

**Test functions created:**
- `is_checkbox_line()` - Recognizes valid checkbox lines
- `get_checkbox_status()` - Returns status (incomplete/complete/failed)
- `extract_checkbox_text()` - Extracts task description
- `get_indentation_level()` - Calculates indentation level

All 16 tests were added to `task-helpers/tests/test_task_parser.py` and verified to fail (red phase), confirming they are non-trivial and will validate the implementation once the functions are created.

The task file has been updated to mark task 2.2 as complete [x], and the "Relevant Files" section has been updated to reflect the checkbox recognition tests.

